    <h2 id="types" style="color:var(--primary);margin-top:40px">Types of Knee Replacement Surgery at DHS</h2>
    <p>The right type of knee replacement depends on which compartments of your knee are damaged, the underlying diagnosis, your age and activity level, and bone quality. Our surgeons offer the full range:</p>

    <div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(260px,1fr));gap:18px;margin-top:18px">
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:var(--radius);padding:22px">
        <h3 style="color:var(--primary);font-size:1.05rem;font-family:'Inter',sans-serif">Total Knee Replacement (TKR)</h3>
        <p style="font-size:.92rem;color:var(--text-light);margin-top:8px">Resurfaces all three compartments of the knee — medial, lateral, and patellofemoral. The most common knee replacement procedure for advanced osteoarthritis, rheumatoid arthritis, or post-traumatic arthritis affecting the whole joint. Available as VELYS robotic-assisted TKR or conventional TKR.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:var(--radius);padding:22px">
        <h3 style="color:var(--primary);font-size:1.05rem;font-family:'Inter',sans-serif">Partial / Uni-condylar Knee Replacement</h3>
        <p style="font-size:.92rem;color:var(--text-light);margin-top:8px">Resurfaces only the damaged compartment of the knee (typically the medial side), preserving healthy bone, ligaments, and cartilage. Smaller incision, faster recovery, more natural-feeling knee. Robotic precision is especially valuable for partial knee replacement because of the small resection volume.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:var(--radius);padding:22px">
        <h3 style="color:var(--primary);font-size:1.05rem;font-family:'Inter',sans-serif">Revision Knee Replacement</h3>
        <p style="font-size:.92rem;color:var(--text-light);margin-top:8px">A second surgery to replace a previously implanted knee that has worn out, loosened, become infected, or developed instability. Requires specialised revision implants and is performed by senior arthroplasty surgeons at DHS.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <h2 id="robotic" style="color:var(--primary);margin-top:40px">Robotic Knee Replacement vs Conventional Knee Replacement</h2>
    <p>DHS offers both robotic-assisted and conventional knee replacement. We recommend <strong>VELYS robotic knee replacement</strong> as the default for most candidates because of improved alignment accuracy and ligament balance — both proven drivers of long-term implant survival and patient satisfaction.</p>

