      {q:"How do I choose between total knee replacement and partial knee replacement?", a:"The decision depends on which compartments of your knee are damaged. If arthritis is limited to one compartment (typically the medial side) and your ligaments are intact, partial / uni-condylar knee replacement preserves healthy bone and provides a more natural-feeling knee with faster recovery. If two or three compartments are affected, total knee replacement is the better choice. Your surgeon will recommend the right option after examining X-rays and assessing ligament integrity."},
