      {q:"Is knee replacement surgery covered by insurance and cashless processing?", a:"Yes. Knee replacement surgery — total, partial, robotic, and revision — is covered by most Indian health insurance policies and TPAs. DHS is empaneled with all major insurers and offers cashless processing through our insurance desk."},
      {q:"How long is recovery after knee replacement surgery?", a:"Most patients stand and walk aided on day 0, are discharged in 2–3 days, walk without aids in 1–2 weeks, return to daily activities including driving in 4–6 weeks, and reach full recovery with complete range of motion at 3–4 months. Robotic-assisted knee replacement typically allows slightly earlier comfortable mobilisation than conventional technique."},
